{"id":319,"flavor":[{"games":["Shield"],"text":"This Pokémon is known as the Bully of the Sea. Any ship entering the waters Sharpedo calls home will be attacked—no exceptions."},{"games":["Sword"],"text":"As soon as it catches the scent of prey, Sharpedo will jet seawater from its backside, hurtling toward the target to attack at 75 mph."},{"games":["Ultra Moon"],"text":"It drinks in seawater and jets it from its rear to propel itself. It’s very sensitive to the scent of blood."},{"games":["Ultra Sun"],"text":"People believe that carrying one of its discarded fangs will prevent mishaps at sea, so the fangs are made into accessories."},{"games":["Moon"],"text":"It has a sad history. In the past, its dorsal fin was a treasured foodstuff, so this Pokémon became a victim of overfishing."},{"games":["Sun"],"text":"It pursues its prey at speeds of 75 mph and finishes them off with fangs that can crush iron. It is known as the bully of the sea."},{"games":["Alpha Sapphire","Sapphire"],"text":"Sharpedo can swim at speeds of up to 75 mph by jetting seawater out of its backside. This Pokémon’s drawback is its inability to swim long distances."},{"games":["Omega Ruby","Ruby"],"text":"Nicknamed “the bully of the sea,” Sharpedo is widely feared. Its cruel fangs grow back immediately if they snap off. Just one of these Pokémon can thoroughly tear apart a supertanker."},{"games":["Y","SoulSilver","HeartGold"],"text":"It can swim at speeds of 75 mph by jetting seawater through its body. It is the bandit of the sea."},{"games":["X","White 2","Black 2","White","Black","Platinum","Pearl","Diamond"],"text":"Its fangs rip through sheet iron. It swims at 75 mph and is known as “The Bully of the Sea.”"},{"games":["LeafGreen","FireRed"],"text":"The ruffian of the seas, it has fangs that crunch through iron. It swims by jetting water from its rear."},{"games":["Emerald"],"text":"The vicious and sly gangster of the sea. Its skin is specially textured to minimize drag in water. Its speed tops out at over 75 miles per hour."}],"abilities":[{"name":"Rough Skin","hidden":false,"description":"The Pokémon's rough skin damages attackers that make direct contact with it."},{"name":"Speed Boost","hidden":true,"description":"The Pokémon's Speed stat is boosted every turn."}],"eggGroups":["Water 2"],"genderRate":4,"hatchCounter":20,"baseHappiness":35,"growthRate":"slow","habitat":"sea","color":"Blue","shape":"Fish","evolution":{"id":318,"name":"Carvanha","condition":null,"children":[{"id":319,"name":"Sharpedo","condition":"Lv. 30","children":[]}]},"moves":{"game":"Sword / Shield","level":[[0,163],[1,43],[1,116],[1,305],[1,400],[1,453],[12,184],[16,44],[20,423],[24,103],[28,207],[34,242],[40,97],[46,710],[52,36]],"machine":[97,372,213,419,59,340,362,523,370,242,399,291,89,203,263,116,416,258,56,63,58,423,196,710,371,398,182,706,240,156,514,317,496,503,184,103,214,555,173,164,57,129,269,168,253,127,250,428],"egg":[],"tutor":[812,799]},"cards":[{"id":"me2-127","name":"Mega Sharpedo ex","set":"Phantasmal Flames","date":"2025-11-14","rarity":"Special Illustration Rare","number":"127","artist":"nagimiso","img":"me2/127"},{"id":"me2-61","name":"Mega Sharpedo ex","set":"Phantasmal Flames","date":"2025-11-14","rarity":"Double Rare","number":"61","artist":"5ban Graphics","img":"me2/61"},{"id":"me2-113","name":"Mega Sharpedo ex","set":"Phantasmal Flames","date":"2025-11-14","rarity":"Ultra Rare","number":"113","artist":"5ban Graphics","img":"me2/113"},{"id":"sv5-43","name":"Sharpedo","set":"Temporal Forces","date":"2024-03-22","rarity":"Uncommon","number":"43","artist":"Shinji Kanda","img":"sv5/43"},{"id":"sv3-47","name":"Sharpedo","set":"Obsidian Flames","date":"2023-08-11","rarity":"Uncommon","number":"47","artist":"Tonji Matsuno","img":"sv3/47"},{"id":"swsh8-163","name":"Sharpedo","set":"Fusion Strike","date":"2021-11-12","rarity":"Uncommon","number":"163","artist":"Hasuno","img":"swsh8/163"},{"id":"swsh7-36","name":"Sharpedo","set":"Evolving Skies","date":"2021-08-27","